WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.633
As for the former

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:02.635
president, he briefly took the stand

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:03.837
today in the witness

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:04.471
stand in the New York

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:05.772
civil fraud trial,

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:07.140
came at the judge's orders

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.441
after the defendant said that.

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:09.909
He said this during a break

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:10.643
in testimony

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:11.911
by his former lawyer and fixer,

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:14.481
Michael Cohen.

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:17.917
This judge is a very partizan judge

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:19.552
with a person who's very partizan

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:20.520
sitting alongside

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.055
and perhaps

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:26.526
even much more partizan than he is.

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:26.993
As you know,

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:27.594
the former president

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:28.795
is already under a gag order

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:31.898
barring him from attacking the judge

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:34.000
and the judge's staff in particular,

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.035
the judge's clerk.

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:36.970
He's already been fined $5,000

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.671
for violating that order.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.106
So when the court return,

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:41.808
the judge called him to the stand

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:43.043
where Trump insisted

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:45.712
he was not talking about the clerk

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.147
who sits to the judge's right.

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:48.481
Instead, the former president claimed

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:49.816
he was referring to Michael Cohen

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:51.251
in the witness chair,

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:53.686
to the judge, to the judge's left.

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:54.421
Now the judge

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:55.188
replying, quote,

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:57.090
I find that the witness is not credible

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.959
and finding him $10,000 in response.

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:00.593
Joining us now,

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:02.395
senior legal and legal analyst,

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:03.463
former criminal defense attorney

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:04.531
Joey Jackson,

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:06.132
and CNN's Kaitlan Collins, host,

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:06.633
The source

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:08.701
coming up at the top of the next hour.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:09.169
So, Joey,

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:11.171
how unusual is it for a judge

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:12.272
to haul a civil defendant

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:13.840
up to the witness stand?

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.375
Listen to what he has to say

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:16.443
and then deem him

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:19.846
not credible and find him?

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:22.082
Yeah, Anderson, it doesn't happen

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:24.384
that often. And obviously it does happen.

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:25.318
It happened here.

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:27.387
But it is certainly a significant step

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:28.755
for a judge to do that.

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:30.356
And so think about what happened here.

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:30.990
Number one,

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.792
the judge issued a determination

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.060
that there was a violation

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.462
of the gag order.

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:37.697
But more importantly, the judge held Mr.

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:39.899
Trump accountable for that violation,

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:40.900
accountable to the tune

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:42.001
of what he understands,

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.169
and that is money.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.704
And so I think what the judge

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.272
is doing by doing that

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:48.842
and get to the credibility determination

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:50.677
momentarily is saying, look,

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:51.644
what I say matters.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:52.512
If there's a gag order,

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:53.546
are you going to follow it?

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:54.981
And so I'm going to hold you accountable

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:56.416
now and I'm going to deter

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:58.218
you in the future from even thinking

00:01:58.218 --> 00:01:59.752
about violating my order

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:02.188
as to the finding of no credibility

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:03.056
by Mr. Trump.

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:05.158
That's huge to think about the case

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:06.659
we're talking about credibility

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:08.061
is everything in a case like this

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:09.429
where you're running a company

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:11.531
and you're alleged to have engaged

00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:12.899
in persistent fraud.

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:13.900
If a judge deems

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.301
you not credible for something

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:17.270
as simple as who you're referring to,

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:17.871
think about what

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:19.472
the judge might be believing

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:20.073
with respect

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:22.175
to testimony involving this company

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:23.343
and and the fraud

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:24.511
that they're accused of.

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:27.480
And so a wholly significant development,

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.648
by all accounts,

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:29.249
with respect

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:30.450
to the merits of the case

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.986
and with regards to him not abiding, Mr.

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:34.487
Trump, that is by the order

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.256
that the judge imposed.

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:37.657
Take a look at the body.

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:38.191
And, Caitlin,

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:38.591
any sense

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:39.626
how this is going over

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:41.161
in the Trump orbit?

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:42.629
Well, I mean, I can guarantee you

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:43.696
that when they all woke up

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:44.430
this morning, Trump's

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:44.998
legal team

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:45.765
and Trump himself,

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:46.466
they did not think

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:47.867
he would actually be called

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:48.968
to the stand today.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.670
But this is a result of, you know,

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.405
nearly every day when he is gone

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:54.707
into the courtroom here in Manhattan.

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:56.442
He has spoken to reporters

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:58.044
railing against the attorney general

00:02:58.044 --> 00:02:58.711
here in New York,

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:01.080
going off on the judge, of course,

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.182
what the judge believed,

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:02.715
going off

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:04.250
on one of his law clerks again

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:05.985
today after he had already

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:07.053
posted pictures of her.

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:07.720
That was the reason

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:08.821
he got that first sign.

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:10.590
It was kind of seen as a technicality

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:11.658
because he left the post

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:13.359
up on his campaign website

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:15.094
but deleted it from his truth social.

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:16.829
And I think the 15 grand

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.464
is not something that you know,

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:19.532
is obviously going to hurt

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:21.401
someone like a Donald Trump.

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:22.635
But it is the essence of it

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:23.369
that he is now

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:24.470
facing punishment

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.372
for the comments that he is making.

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:27.273
And he got up there

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:28.841
and tried to make his own argument,

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:29.809
try to argue

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:30.577
that he wasn't

00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:32.011
actually talking

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.313
about this law clerk,

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:34.480
even though the judge noted

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.882
she's had a lot closer to him

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:36.849
than Michael Cohen did,

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.384
who was in the witness stand.

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:39.619
And the judge quickly

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:40.520
did not believe him.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:41.554
And I think this is the first time

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:42.922
we've seen Donald Trump actually

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:44.857
testifying in an open court

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.659
in more than a decade.

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:48.428
And he is expected to actually testify

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:49.062
in this trial

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:51.030
not related to this matter, Anderson.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.232
And it doesn't seem to bode

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:53.399
well for what that testimony

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:55.868
is going to look like.

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:56.836
And given the fact that

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:58.371
he is attending this continues

00:03:58.371 --> 00:03:59.906
to attend this trial.

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:00.873
I know there were some days

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:01.441
he wasn't there,

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:02.408
but it's

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:02.742
I mean, it's

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:04.477
just a sign of how important

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:06.746
he thinks this is. It's personal.

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:08.381
It is incredibly personal for him.

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:09.482
That is why he is

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:11.517
I mean, he's flying up here from Florida

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:12.151
to come to this.

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:12.752
It's not like he's

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:14.387
just hanging out in New Jersey

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:15.221
at his nearby club.

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:15.855
I mean, he is

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:17.190
he went back to Florida today

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.225
after leaving that courtroom earlier

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:21.427
and he has sat in on it multiple days.

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:22.428
He is not,

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:22.629
you know,

00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:23.563
just sitting there quietly

00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:25.164
paying attention to the proceedings.

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:26.366
We've I've heard

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:27.734
from our reporters in the room,

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:28.001
you know,

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:29.369
he's at times throwing his hands

00:04:29.369 --> 00:04:30.136
up in the air,

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:31.204
kind of rolling his eyes

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:32.305
at the proceedings.

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:33.206
Him and Michael Cohen

00:04:33.206 --> 00:04:34.440
being in the same courtroom

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.309
in and of itself is something shocking.

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:36.876
I don't think they've been

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:38.278
in the same room together

00:04:38.278 --> 00:04:39.379
in about five years.

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:40.079
And Michael Cohen

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:41.047
was in there, obviously,

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:41.814
and we've seen

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:42.715
how their relationship

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:43.783
has completely devolved

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:45.518
into and deteriorated.

00:04:45.518 --> 00:04:47.253
And it's just remarkable to see,

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:47.720
you know,

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:48.788
that this is something

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:49.789
he really cares about.

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:50.523
The outcome of this,

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:51.457
even though largely it's

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:54.560
already kind of been decided.

00:04:54.661 --> 00:04:55.128
And, Joe,

00:04:55.128 --> 00:04:56.129
what happens if he

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:57.463
runs afoul of the gag order?

00:04:57.463 --> 00:04:59.732
Again?

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:01.601
Yeah, I think the judge is setting

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:02.635
the tone, Anderson,

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:04.270
as it relates to what he expects

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:05.204
and anticipates.

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:06.906
This is not a broad, hard

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:08.975
to follow gag order. It's a gag order.

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:11.010
And as much as the judge said, listen,

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:13.246
staff is off limits, do not address that.

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:14.013
He did.

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:15.181
And so what

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:16.549
the judge did, I think, is in

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:18.918
keeping with what judges like to do,

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:20.687
and that is ensure decorum, ensure

00:05:20.687 --> 00:05:22.021
that orders are followed,

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:23.923
ensure that people are not attacked

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:25.992
or demean for simply doing their job.

00:05:25.992 --> 00:05:27.560
And it's really setting the stage

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:28.795
for moving forward

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:29.862
that if you do it again

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:30.963
and again, deterrence,

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:31.631
that I'm going to have

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:32.598
something to say about it.

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:33.633
And so I think we could see

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:35.601
fines that increase

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:37.203
and continue to increase.

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:38.338
And remember briefly

00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:39.972
this is not the first time

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:40.740
in connection

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:42.508
with this case that he was fine.

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:44.610
He was fined because of not complying

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:45.445
with handing over

00:05:45.445 --> 00:05:47.447
information to the attorney general,

00:05:47.447 --> 00:05:49.916
to the tune of over $100,000.

00:05:49.916 --> 00:05:51.651
And I just would add that in a case

00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:52.919
where a judge is making

00:05:52.919 --> 00:05:54.721
a judicial determination

00:05:54.721 --> 00:05:56.356
about whether you're responsible

00:05:56.356 --> 00:05:56.956
and certainly

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:58.591
your licenses are at stake

00:05:58.591 --> 00:05:59.959
in the state of New York

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:00.793
and what you do

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:02.161
and your business practices

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:03.496
and what the findings are.

00:06:03.496 --> 00:06:04.931
I think he's the last person

00:06:04.931 --> 00:06:06.766
that you might want to get upset

00:06:06.766 --> 00:06:07.867
and who you might want to

00:06:07.867 --> 00:06:09.535
not follow their orders.

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:11.137
And so we'll see whether Mr.

00:06:11.137 --> 00:06:12.739
Trump could comply with that

00:06:12.739 --> 00:06:13.439
moving forward.

